The attached image, Figure 5 from the PDF, demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A shows flow cytometry dot plots where BMDCs incubated with soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) alone display modest OVA uptake, but when OVA is adsorbed to AF647-labeled Nano-11, a significantly higher percentage of cells become positive for both OVA and Nano-11. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, further illustrates this, showing a substantial shift to higher fluorescence intensity for cells treated with Nano-11+OVA compared to OVA alone, confirming enhanced antigen delivery to DCs, a critical step for immune activation.